Subject: [PATCH] modelblaster: per-channel MBP kernels, and the integer nonlinearities

Four things, all at pipeline's own documented extension points, so that what
fpga/pynq-z2/sw/int_nonlin.c measures becomes a property of a model ModelBlaster can
emit rather than a property of a benchmark.  Curated kernels themselves live OUTSIDE the
submodule, at fpga/pynq-z2/modelblaster/kernels/{pext,pext_nl}/, reached with
--global-curated-dir, exactly as patches/0009 arranged.

1. pipeline/backends.py -- one Backend named "pext_nl": MBP plus the integer softmax,
   layer norm, GELU and matmul-requantise kernels.

   It is a SEPARATE backend rather than a flag on `pext` because `pext` declares
   atol_override = rtol_override = 0.0 and means it.  The integer replacements cannot be
   bit-exact against a reference written in expf, double and roundf, and shipping them
   under `pext` would mean widening that backend's tolerance for every op it has --
   retiring the strongest claim in this project to buy a convenience.  pext_nl's
   tolerance is 2.0, which is the MEASURED worst int8 output difference (Lab B20) and
   not a round number, and `--max-accuracy-class bit_exact` still tightens the
   convolution and fully-connected kernels back to atol 0 on it.

   curated_aliases = ("pext",), so pext_nl inherits every pext kernel rather than
   needing a second copy -- and, per backend_lineage's own docstring, inherits the conv
   weight-layout decision with them.  The three existing pext candidates gain "pext_nl"
   in their target_affinity, because the algorithm-queue filter matches the backend name
   exactly and would otherwise drop them.

2. conv2d_s8_pc and linear_s8_pc get MBP candidates.  SPEECH_ON_ROCKET.md 3.4 measured
   per-channel weight scales at +3.62 accuracy points on kws_cnn over all 5,274 held-out
   clips, and recorded that they could not be used at all, because --per-channel renames
   the ops and the curated kernels were registered for the per-tensor names only: the
   choice on offer was 3.6 points of accuracy OR 25x of speed, with nothing in between.
   Both new kernels are the per-tensor ones with the requantise descriptor turned into
   an array indexed by output channel; everything expensive is untouched.  Bit-exact,
   checked over 24,006 conv and 4,272 linear output elements against the _pc reference.

3. gelu_s8 gets two candidates, and the bit-exact one is the surprise: with per-tensor
   symmetric quantisation gelu_s8 is a pointwise map from 256 input bytes to 256 output
   bytes, so evaluating erff once per ELEMENT is never necessary whatever arithmetic it
   is evaluated in.  Lab B19 measured the reference at 3,093 cycles/element on a
   131,072-element ffn_block activation -- 405 million cycles to evaluate a 256-entry
   function.  pext_memo_lut is 31 cycles/element, bit-exact.  pext_int_lut removes the
   remaining 256 erff calls too: 20 cycles/element, 1 int8 LSB, and input-independent.

4. softmax_s8, layernorm_s8 and matmul_s8 get the integer kernels int_nonlin.c already
   measured at 32.9x, 16.6x and 4.6x on the silicon.  matmul_s8 is the one nobody had
   looked at, because it LOOKS integer: its reduction is int32 and its tail is one
   roundf((float)acc * total) per output element, measured at 244 cycles on this
   WithoutFPU core (37 in integer, 6.6x), paid heads*T*T times per attention layer.

Applied by scripts/39_rocket_xformer_cost.sh --target pext_nl and by
scripts/40_rocket_int_nonlin.sh.  Depends on patches/0009 being applied first.  NOT
upstream.

diff --git a/pipeline/backends.py b/pipeline/backends.py
--- a/pipeline/backends.py	2026-09-16 16:52:41.833526640 -0700
+++ b/pipeline/backends.py	2026-09-16 17:21:56.809206162 -0700
@@ -635,6 +635,55 @@
 )
 
 
+# MBP plus the INTEGER nonlinearities of fpga/pynq-z2/sw/int_nonlin.c.
+#
+# WHY IT IS A SEPARATE BACKEND AND NOT A FLAG ON `pext`.  The pext backend declares
+# atol_override = rtol_override = 0.0, and it means it: every curated kernel for it
+# recomputes the reference expression in the same rounding mode and every shape it
+# cannot accelerate falls through to the reference verbatim.  The integer softmax,
+# layer norm, GELU and matmul requantise CANNOT be bit-exact against a reference
+# written in `expf`, `double` and `roundf`, and they do not claim to be.  Shipping them
+# under `pext` would mean widening that backend's tolerance for every op it has, which
+# would retire the strongest claim in this project.  So they get their own name, its
+# tolerance is the MEASURED worst int8 output difference rather than a round number,
+# and `pext` is unchanged.
+#
+# WHAT THE TOLERANCE IS AND WHERE IT COMES FROM.  Lab B20 (scripts/40_rocket_int_nonlin.sh)
+# measures each replacement on the silicon against the reference expression compiled into
+# the same image, and reports the worst int8 OUTPUT difference, because that is all a
+# downstream layer can see:
+#
+#     softmax_s8    32.9x   2 LSB  (1 LSB for the reference's own p/scale_out encoding)
+#     layernorm_s8  16.6x   1 LSB
+#     gelu_s8      262x     1 LSB, and its ENTIRE 256-value input domain enumerated
+#     matmul_s8 requantise tail   6.6x   1 LSB
+#
+# 2 LSB on a 255-level encoding is 0.8% of full scale, on a quantity the next layer
+# immediately requantises.  `--max-accuracy-class bit_exact` still tightens the
+# convolution and fully-connected kernels back to atol 0 on this backend, because that
+# filter only ever tightens.
+#
+# curated_aliases = ("pext",) so this backend inherits every pext kernel rather than
+# needing a second copy of them -- and, per backend_lineage's own docstring, inherits
+# the conv weight layout decision with them.  Without it every op would silently fall
+# back to the scalar reference and the build would still report success.
+PEXT_NL = Backend(
+    name="pext_nl",
+    description=(
+        "rv64imac + MBP (as `pext`) plus the integer softmax / layer norm / GELU / "
+        "matmul-requantise kernels of fpga/pynq-z2/sw/int_nonlin.c. Same hart-0 "
+        "pinning contract as pext; numeric_drift on the four nonlinear ops, bounded "
+        "and measured at 1-2 int8 LSB."
+    ),
+    kernel_cflags=("-DMB_PEXT_HW=1",),
+    optimization_guide="optimization_guide_scalar.md",
+    verify_method=VERIFY_HOST_CTYPES,
+    curated_aliases=("pext",),
+    atol_override=2.0,
+    rtol_override=0.0,
+)
+
+
 RVV_HETERO = Backend(
     name="rvv_hetero",
     description=(
@@ -664,6 +713,7 @@
     GEMMINI_Q31.name: GEMMINI_Q31,
     GEMMINI_Q31_RVV.name: GEMMINI_Q31_RVV,
     PEXT.name: PEXT,
+    PEXT_NL.name: PEXT_NL,
 }
 
 
